@53   = ~Quiet Slippers~
@54   = ~These slippers are very comfortable and, because of how soft they are, they allow one to move without making too much noise. But they also look quite neat; they are somewhat fluffy.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Move Silently: +5%

Weight: 2~
@55   = ~Ink Gallery: The List of Exhibits~
@56   = ~The list includes all books that are currently presented to people. These are:

– Tale of the Eight-Legged Strider: a story about a group wading through the Demonweb Pits, trying to leave the domain of the Spider Queen.

– The Birth of the Fury: a tale from far Kara-Tur, about Chin Yi, as well as a swordsman from Shou Lung, and their love.

– The Deathly Groans: this novella presents a dreadful tale of a necromancer and an army of undead xvarts he decided to raise from their slumber.

– The War Below: this tale tells the story of one of the lesser-known adventures of the Heroes of Icewind Dale and how, during their attempt to stop a war between strange beings, they discovered a cave, home to a huge and quite dangerous creature.

– The Grasp of the Glabrezu: this cautionary tale describes a fight between a glabrezu, protected by bow-wielding devilesses, and a group of adventurers that were sent to Avernus to find and kill that glabrezu.

– The Dance of the Swords: the book describes a ball organized by a mysterious Maestro, and an unusual dance of literal swords, controlled by the bard.

– Of Seed & Fire: a story about an angry fire giant druid, who claimed a significant part of the bog and attacks those that dare to enter it.

– The Story of the Moon Sisters: a tale about three celestial sisters, the judges that live in a strange moon-like place, covered with silver sands.

– Tale of the Dead Eye: a novel in which a lone traveler has to travel through a strange place, a dead magic zone, and encounters a zombie beholder, hungry and angered, ready to attack.

– The Three Thirsty Rascals: a somewhat experimental story, a macabre comedy about three kobold vampires that terrorize a nearby village.

– The Waves of Flesheaters: a book that describes the struggle of a lone survivor walking down an old sewer system, where he has to face dozens of flesh-eating maggots hiding in the murky water and shadows.

– The Light in the Snow: a story of an old remorhaz roaming the far north, accompanied by creatures that seem like sentient winds.

All interested in learning more from these tales are welcome to visit the Ink Gallery and check the books with their own eyes.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 1~
@57   = ~Ink Gallery: Testimonials~
@58   = ~This pamphlet shows some drawings of the Ink Gallery located in Athkatla, in the Government District. It also includes some testimonials left by other customers: 

"Some of those stories are truly marvelous! While they are a great opportunity to learn, remember to prepare yourself first!"
- Brienda Falcontrade, Shield-Bearer from Neverwinter

"The Ink Gallery taught me that literature may come with many thrills and excitements! Thank you for that!"
- Al'Mand Silloan, Priest of Helm from Calimport

"I never liked books and now—I think they're great!"
- John Bubblovich, a fashion figure from... somewhere!

STATISTICS:

Weight: 1~
@59   = ~Flail~
@60   = ~Priestess' Emasculator +3~
@61   = ~This weapon was once a favorite weapon of a drow priestess. She was a cruel matron, known for her hatred of men—even for drow standards. She liked to torture them, and make it all a spectacle for other men to observe. They say it was her way to emasculate not just one man, but all of them, all at once.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Immunity to Poison

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d6+4, +1d4+1 Acid vs. Males
Damage type: Crushing
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Flail/Morning Star
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 9 Strength

Weight: 10~
@62   = ~Horn~
@63   = ~Trumpet of Delirious Celebrations~
@64   = ~Tales say that this trumpet once belonged to one of Kwan Ying's archons, a fellow of Chin Yi, another archon that later became the source of the Celestial Fury's true power. People say that when the Trumpet of Delirious Celebrations is blown, people around start acting as if they were drunk and find it difficult to hit the user of this instrument.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Delirious Celebration once per day
  Special: Enemies in the radius must pass a save vs. spells at -4 or suffer from powerful magical drunkenness that lasts 5 turns. For those that fail the save, there is also a 5% chance to fall onto the ground unconscious for 2 rounds. The character that blows the instrument is also granted +1 Armor Class and +1 Charisma bonuses for the whole duration.
  Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius

Weight: 2~
@65   = ~Bracers~
@66   = ~Bracelets of the Xvart Necromancer~
@67   = ~These bracelets used to belong to a powerful xvart necromancer. It's hard to say how it was possible for someone like him to become a true master of dark magic, but it happened. He managed to raise many of his fallen kin by turning them into the living dead.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: 7
– Constitution: +1
– Can memorize one extra arcane spell of each level from 1st to 3rd (necromancer only)

Weight: 1~
@68   = ~Titanic Lava Ankheg Plate~
@69   = ~This plate armor was created from a titanic lava ankheg shell. While lava ankhegs are quite rare, the titanic version of the creature must have been somewhat unique. It was huge and powerful, and it could spit some corrosive substance. But even that could not save it from death.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Fire Resistance: +30%
– Physical Damage Resistance: +5%

Armor Class: 0 (-3 vs. slashing, -1 vs. piercing and missile)
Requires:
 8 Strength

Weight: 25~
@70   = ~Belt~
@71   = ~Glabrezu's Arousal~
@72   = ~If tales are to be believed, this belt was created from the skin and bones of a powerful glabrezu, feared by both mortals and other devils. He was said to feel sadistic arousal from killing all those that were ready to stand in his way.

It looks like this belt also has some parasitic properties, and that it is blood that channels the belt's magic. The diabolical nature of this weapon does not allow paladins to wear it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Magic Resistance: +8%
– Attacks per round: +1/2
– THAC0: +1
– Constitution: -1
– May only be removed with a Remove Curse spell

Weight: 2~
@73   = ~Scimitar~
@74   = ~Maestro's Aeon +3~
@75   = ~There are many magical scimitars that would be happily used by bards and other artists. This one, however, has quite a reputation. It is not only a well-crafted weapon, but also one that was enchanted with quite interesting magic. It allows the user to regenerate and affect both the wielder's and the target's ability to withstand magic attacks.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Regenerates 1 Hit Point every two rounds

Combat abilities:
– Each successful hit drains Saving Throws vs. Magic for 1 round (each hit lowers the target's Save vs. Magic by 1 point, and that same Save of the weapon wielder is improved by 1; the effect stacks)

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d8+3 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: Scimitar/Wakizashi/Ninjatō
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 10 Strength

Weight: 3~
@76   = ~Ring~
@77   = ~Fire Rowan Ring~
@78   = ~This ring was made using dried fire rowan, and enchanted with powerful magic. Tales say it was created by a powerful yet quite mad druid, a fire giant that tried to claim part of the bog for himself.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +2
– Saving Throws: +2

Charge abilities:
– Fire Seed once per day
  Effect: Creates 4 fire seeds that will appear in the caster's inventory. The seeds will remain in existence for 3 turns after the spell is cast. If they are thrown at an enemy, a fireball will ensue, causing 2d8 points of damage to all within a 7-ft. radius unless they make a Saving Throw vs. Spell for half damage.

Weight: 1~
@79   = ~Small Shield~
@80   = ~Three Moon Phases +3~
@81   = ~This small shield was created by winged celestial beings, the Moon Sisters. If legends are true, each of them was responsible for one part of this shield, and then they were put together, creating an unusual piece of gear that's even more impressive during the nighttime.

The shield, while it does not protect from missiles in the usual way, can weaken projectiles by burning them with moonlight.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +4
– Does not provide an Armor Class bonus against missile attacks
– Missile Damage Resistance: 50%
– Magic Resistance: +3%

Special abilities:
– During nighttime, each round, the wielder of the shield gains one of three additional bonuses at random: +1 Luck, Regeneration (3 Hit Points over 1 round), or Protection from Petrification.

Requires:
 4 Strength

Weight: 2~
@82   = ~Ioun Stone~
@83   = ~Dead Levitating Eye~
@84   = ~This unusual ioun stone was shaped to look like a glass eye, or dead eye, thus its name: Dead Levitating Eye. It can magically help one see what's usually hard to spot, thus rogues will get the most from using it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Detect Traps: +10%
– Detect Illusion: +10%
– Ranged THAC0: +1

Weight: 0~
@85   = ~Dart~
@86   = ~Little Rascal's Tooth +2~
@87   = ~This dart is actually a polished and enchanted vampiric tooth turned into a weapon. If tales are to be believed, the tooth still has some interesting vampiric properties.

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
